<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  <meta name="version" content="WD-excerpt-2"/>
  <title>W3C Sample API Excerpt</title>
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/sample-api/"/>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="head">
    <p>W3C Working Draft</p>
    <p class="copyright">Copyright © W3C corpus excerpt for offline regression.</p>
  </div>
  <nav id="toc"><ol><li>Introduction</li></ol></nav>
  <main id="main">
    <h1>Sample API (W3C-style corpus)</h1>
    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>This document models W3C TR HTML structure for NormShift M1.</p>
    <h2>2. Conformance</h2>
    <p id="c1">Implementations MUST support the open() method.</p>
    <p id="c2">User agents MUST display a warning when certificates are invalid.</p>
    <section class="informative">
      <h3>Informative note</h3>
      <p>Authors MUST NOT treat informative sections as requirements.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="example">
      <p>Example: the client MUST send Accept headers in this sample only.</p>
    </div>
    <h2>3. Security Considerations</h2>
    <p>Discussions here are non-extractable by section policy in M1 corpus design.</p>
    <h2>4. Networking</h2>
    <p id="c3">Clients MUST NOT send credentials on cross-origin redirects.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
